    {
      "id": "TCM-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "The double commutant of the place permutations is their own span",
      "anchor": "inputs-trace-double",
      "statement": "For the unital complex star algebra 𝒜 spanned by P(σ,w), every matrix T commuting with 𝒜′ lies in 𝒜.",
      "hypotheses": "Finite-dimensional complex matrix spaces. The algebra contains the identity, is closed under multiplication and conjugate transpose, and carries the Hilbert–Schmidt inner product.",
      "definitions": [
        "P(σ,w)P(τ,v)=P(σ∘τ,w) if v=w∘σ and zero otherwise.",
        "The adjoint of P(σ,w) is P(σ⁻¹,w∘σ) and the unit is ∑_w P(id,w).",
        "The Hilbert–Schmidt projection Π onto 𝒜 commutes with left multiplication by 𝒜. Its linear blocks from one column to another lie in 𝒜′."
      ],
