    {
      "id": "TCM-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Contracting a place permutation gives one trace for each cycle",
      "anchor": "inputs-trace-cycle-return",
      "statement": "Every real, alternating, unitary-invariant q-form at the identity is a linear combination of unnormalized alternations of real and imaginary parts of products of complex traces, one per permutation cycle at a common place.",
      "hypotheses": "The tangent tuple consists of Hermitian N-by-N matrices at the infinite places of a number field. The tensor span is valid for all N and q. The odd-degree optimal count of tests needs the separate cohomological filtering and reversal argument.",
      "definitions": [
        "With a matrix unit at each input slot the contraction is ∑_I,J T_IJ ∏ᵢ blk(Yᵢ)_(Iᵢ,Jᵢ).",
        "The contraction attached to P(σ,w) vanishes unless w∘σ=w. The operator itself can carry one place pattern to a different one.",
        "If c=a+ib is the complex expansion coefficient, the coefficients of the unnormalized alternating real and imaginary components are a/q! and −b/q!."
      ],
